Sam: Sounds great. What films are they showing?
Mia: On Saturday it''s a story about robots that take over a city.
Sam: Hmm, that sounds a bit scary. What about Sunday?
Mia: Sunday is about a girl who builds a time machine and travels to the future.
Sam: I love time-travel stories. Let''s go on Sunday, then.
Mia: Perfect. I''ll book two tickets online tonight.
Sam: Thanks. Shall we meet at the cinema at two o''clock?', 'Mia 邀 Sam 周末去科幻电影节;周六放机器人占领城市的片子,Sam 觉得有点吓人;周日放一个女孩造时间机器去未来的故事;Sam 爱看时间旅行,决定周日去;Mia 今晚网上订两张票,约定两点在影院碰面。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What event are Mia and Sam talking about?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["A science fiction film festival.","A football match.","A music concert.","A school exam."]},{"q":"What is Saturday''s film about?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["A girl and a time machine.","Robots taking over a city.","A trip to the sea.","A cooking show."]},{"q":"Why does Sam choose the Sunday film?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["He loves time-travel stories.","It is free.","It is shorter.","His friends chose it."]},{"q":"How will Mia get the tickets?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["She will buy them at the door.","She will book them online.","She will ask a friend.","She will not buy any."]},{"q":"When will they meet at the cinema?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["At ten o''clock.","At noon.","At two o''clock.","At midnight."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'elective4', 'U1');
It often describes robots, space travel, time machines, and life on other planets.
Long ago, robots existed only in such stories.
Today many of those imagined ideas are slowly becoming real.
Good science fiction makes us think about how technology may change our lives.', '科幻是一种关于未来和科学的故事;常描写机器人、太空旅行、时间机器和其他星球上的生活;很久以前,机器人只存在于这类故事中;如今许多想象中的点子正慢慢变成现实;好的科幻让我们思考科技会如何改变生活。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What is science fiction mainly about?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Only old history.","Cooking and food.","Sports games.","The future and science."]},{"q":"Which of these does science fiction often describe?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Robots and space travel.","Farm animals only.","School timetables.","Weather reports."]},{"q":"Where did robots exist long ago?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["In every home.","Only in such stories.","In real factories.","On every street."]},{"q":"What is happening to many imagined ideas today?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["They are forgotten.","They are banned.","They are slowly becoming real.","They are sold abroad."]},{"q":"What does good science fiction make us do?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Stop using machines.","Forget the future.","Avoid all science.","Think about how technology may change life."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'short', 'elective4', 'U1');
Expert: Yes, I have two. One helps me cook, and the other cleans the floor.
Host: Interesting! What jobs do you think robots will do in the future?
Expert: I believe they will work in teaching and nursing, helping people every day.
Host: That sounds useful. But could robots also become dangerous?
Expert: As they grow more intelligent, they may also become harder to control.
Host: So the line between humans and robots will get blurred?
Expert: Exactly. That is why clear rules and careful testing matter so much.', '主持人欢迎科幻专家,问他家里有没有机器人;专家有两个,一个帮做饭一个扫地;谈到未来机器人会从事教学和护理;主持人担心机器人也会变危险;专家说它们越聪明越难控制;人机界限会变模糊;因此明确规则和谨慎测试很重要。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"How many robots does the expert have at home?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Two.","Five.","None.","Ten."]},{"q":"What does one of his robots do?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["It drives a car.","It helps him cook.","It writes books.","It plays music."]},{"q":"In which jobs does the expert think robots will work?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Only in factories.","Only in shops.","Teaching and nursing.","Nowhere at all."]},{"q":"Why might robots become dangerous?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["They get cheaper.","They grow smaller.","They use less power.","They grow more intelligent and harder to control."]},{"q":"What does the expert say matters so much?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Clear rules and careful testing.","Buying more robots.","Faster machines.","Cheaper tickets."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'elective4', 'U1');
The first law says a robot must never harm a human being.
The second law says a robot must obey the orders given by people.
But it must not obey an order if that order breaks the first law.
The third law says a robot must protect itself, as long as this does not break the other laws.', '著名作家阿西莫夫制定了三条让机器人安全的定律;第一定律:机器人绝不能伤害人类;第二定律:机器人必须服从人的命令;但若命令违反第一定律则不可服从;第三定律:机器人必须保护自己,只要不违反前两条。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"Who created the three laws of robotics?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Liu Cixin.","Isaac Asimov.","Ken Liu.","H. G. Wells."]},{"q":"What does the first law say a robot must never do?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Speak to humans.","Clean a floor.","Harm a human being.","Charge its battery."]},{"q":"What does the second law tell a robot to do?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Ignore all people.","Run away from humans.","Sleep all day.","Obey the orders given by people."]},{"q":"When must a robot not obey an order?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["When the order breaks the first law.","When it is tired.","When it is busy.","When it is night."]},{"q":"What does the third law allow a robot to do?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Harm anyone it likes.","Protect itself, if it breaks no other law.","Stop working forever.","Disobey every order."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'short', 'elective4', 'U1');
Tom: Really? What can it do for him?
Lucy: It reminds him to take his medicine and reads the news aloud.
Tom: That''s so helpful. Does it ever make mistakes?
Lucy: Sometimes it hears the wrong word, and we all laugh.
Tom: Ha! Is your grandfather worried about it at all?
Lucy: A little. He says a machine must always be kept safe and private.
Tom: That''s a wise point. New technology should help us, not control us.', 'Lucy 的爷爷有了个小型 AI 助手,很棒;它提醒爷爷吃药、朗读新闻;有时听错词逗大家笑;爷爷有点担心,说机器必须保证安全和隐私;Tom 赞同:新技术应帮助我们,而非控制我们。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"Who got the AI helper?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Tom''s brother.","Lucy''s teacher.","Lucy''s grandfather.","Tom''s mother."]},{"q":"What is one thing the AI helper does?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["It cooks dinner.","It drives a car.","It paints pictures.","It reminds him to take his medicine."]},{"q":"Why do they sometimes laugh at the helper?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["It hears the wrong word.","It sings badly.","It falls over.","It runs away."]},{"q":"What is the grandfather a little worried about?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["The colour of the machine.","Keeping it safe and private.","The price of the machine.","The size of the machine."]},{"q":"What do Lucy and Tom agree about technology?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["It is always useless.","It should replace all people.","It should help us, not control us.","It should never be used."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'elective4', 'U1');
First, think of one big idea, such as a robot, an alien, or a time machine.
Next, imagine how your world looks and how your machine works.
Then use vivid words to help readers picture the strange new sights.
Finally, leave a surprising ending so that readers keep thinking about your story.', '给你写科幻故事几个小贴士:先想一个大点子,比如机器人、外星人或时间机器;再想象你的世界长什么样、机器如何运转;然后用生动的词让读者在脑中描绘奇异的新景象;最后留一个出人意料的结尾,让读者回味无穷。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What is the passage mainly about?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["How to repair a robot.","How to buy a ticket.","A weather report.","Tips for writing a sci-fi story."]},{"q":"What should a writer think of first?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["One big idea like a robot or time machine.","A long list of names.","The price of paper.","A song to sing."]},{"q":"Why should a writer use vivid words?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["To make the story shorter.","To help readers picture the new sights.","To save time.","To hide the story."]},{"q":"What kind of ending does the passage suggest?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["A boring ending.","No ending at all.","A surprising ending.","A copied ending."]},{"q":"What will a surprising ending make readers do?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Stop reading at once.","Forget the story.","Throw the book away.","Keep thinking about the story."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'short', 'elective4', 'U1');

